  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A spherical shell of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> mass and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is rolling with angular speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi></math> on horizontal plane (as shown in figure). The magnitude of angular momentum of the shell about the origin <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#969;</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;will be</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0098_196f6a82334f.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 124px;\" />&nbsp;</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\qt0098_196f6a82334f.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 124px;\" /></p><p>Angular momentum of a rotating and translating body is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#969;</mi></math></p><p>For rolling,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>R</mi></math></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>Therefore, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
}